From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:46:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diagnostics: park load timings and the perf log (test builds
 only)

Test-only instrumentation, kept last so a release build drops this one
patch.

Title park loads: each load's stages (read, objects, early registration,
register with ObjectManager's breakdown, import, swap, finish, prepare,
total, in milliseconds) are appended to <user dir>/rct-screensaver-engine.log
and stdout. ObjectManager::GetLastLoadTimings() reports the parts of the
last LoadObjects call.

Perf log: --perf-log <file> writes one line per drawn frame (interval,
ticks, and the time spent in the tick, plugin calls, input, paint and
present, with the main viewport's position, zoom and rotation), a sample
every 10 s (process memory, handles, GDI objects, the QuickJS heap, image
list use and fragmentation, guests, staff, vehicles, litter, all entities,
rides) and events (each title park load's stages, marks from the plugin,
quit). Off and free without the flag. --perf-quit-after <s> ends the run;
--no-background-loading loads title parks the stock way for A/B runs
(TitleSequence.backgroundLoading then reads false).

Plugin API: screensaver.perfLog (bool) and screensaver.perfMark(text).

Read by tools/perfreport.py; runs driven by tools/perfrun.py.
